 object Interpreter:
+  // Cached once, not re-queried on every recursive interpretation step: `sys.env`
+  // rebuilds a whole `Map` from the process environment on every call, and while
+  // that's cheap enough on a real JVM (`System.getenv()` returns an already-parsed,
+  // cached `java.util.Map`) not to matter even hit millions of times, Scala
+  // Native's `System.getenv()`/`sys.env` is measured ~7x more expensive per call
+  // (a 2,000,000-iteration microbenchmark: ~4.8s on JVM vs ~34.8s on Scala Native) --
+  // and this debug gate is checked from ~35 call sites across `interpretTree0`'s own
+  // recursive descent, hit on every node of every macro interpretation. Against a
+  // real, macro-derivation-heavy project (`~/scala/ape`), re-querying `sys.env` on
+  // every step (rather than once here) was severe enough to turn a ~2 minute real
+  // compile into one that hadn't finished after 15+ minutes. The env var can't
+  // change mid-run, so computing this once is always correct, not just a
+  // Scala-Native-specific workaround.
+  private[dotc] val debugEnabled: Boolean = sys.env.contains("SCALINO_INTERP_DEBUG")
+  private[dotc] val debugMatchEnabled: Boolean = sys.env.contains("SCALINO_INTERP_DEBUG_MATCH")
+
